     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\">Hello,</font><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">I ran into a puzzling outcome while using lavaan and hoped to get another perspective on the issue. I am new to lavaan, but have experience with path-analysis.</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">I constructed a simple model with observed variables: B causes both A and C (diagram below). </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">A, B, and C are the only variables in the model, and the only paths are B&gt;A and B&gt;C. No covariance between A and C is specified. This model should have 1 degree of freedom because the association between A and C is expected to be the product of paths B&gt;A and B&gt;C, which can be compared to the observed association to test model fit.</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Although I believe I specified the model correctly, lavaan did not use the association between A and C to test model fit, rather, the output shows a model with 0 degrees of freedom. I am puzzled by this and wondering if someone with more experience could weigh in, or suggest better ways of using lavaan for path-analysis.</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Thanks in advance for any help. Here is the code, the relevant output, and the diagram:</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><b>CODE</b>:</font></div><div><div><font color=\"#000000\">mod1 &lt;-&#39;</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">A ~ a1*B</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">C ~ a2*B</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">&#39;</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">mod1_fit &lt;- sem(mod1,data=data1)</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">summary(mod1_fit, fit.measures = TRUE, modindices = TRUE, standardized = TRUE, rsquare = TRUE)</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><font color=\"#000000\">Relevant Output:</font></b></span></p><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">lavaan (0.5-23.1097) converged normally after  20 iterations<u></u><u></u></font></span></pre><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><u></u><font color=\"#000000\"> </font><u></u></span></pre><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">                                                  Used       Total<u></u><u></u></font></span></pre><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">  Number of observations                          2246        2249<u></u><u></u></font></span></pre><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\"><u></u><font color=\"#000000\"> </font><u></u></span></pre><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:init