   "subject": "Re: lavaan removing degree of freedom? (unspecified endogenous covariance)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The default behavior for the sem function is to covary residuals for endogenous variables (see the help file for the sem function ?sem for details). In particular the option auto.cov.y is set to true. To turn off this behavior you can set auto.cov.y=FALSE in the sem command, explicitly set the covariance of a and c to zero in the syntax, or use the lavaan function (which has fewer defaults).<div><br></div><div>Alex</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
